===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|baseball|slang|rare}} A foul ball which just brushes by the bat, making a ticking sound.
#: ''The catcher held onto the '''foul tick''' for the out.''

Commonly used Midwestern, mid-20th century term, particularly in pick up baseball games with no umpires. A refinement of the foul tip, where the ball is hit by the bat but has no visible change of direction, it was generally decalred by saying "Tick! I heard it!' All foul ticks are foul tips, but not all foul tips are foul ticks.

